★★★ THE SECOND ASSEMBLY DIALECT, EXECUTING. A hand-written AArch64 `.s` — no C anywhere, and not one byte of it lexable by the x86_64 AT&T dialect — goes text → CST → LIR → machine words → linked ELF → RUNS UNDER qemu-aarch64, exiting 42. Its sibling `asm_arith_return42` proved the mechanism once; this file is what turns 'assembly is its own language' from a design into a measured reuse claim, because the shared line grammar in `asm.lang.json` received a genuinely different dialect WITHOUT CHANGING.

★★★ WHAT MAKES IT A REAL TEST RATHER THAN THE FIRST EXAMPLE WITH RENAMED MNEMONICS. Every axis a 'shared token table with knobs' design would have had to parameterise is different here, and two of them are single bytes whose meanings are INVERTED between the two dialects:
  • `#` opens an IMMEDIATE here and a LINE COMMENT there;
  • `%` opens the TYPE marker here (`%function`) and a REGISTER there (`%rax`);
  • comments are `//` here, `#` there;
  • registers carry NO sigil here (`x0`), a `%` there;
  • memory is `[base, #off]` here, `disp(base,index,scale)` there;
  • operand order is destination-FIRST here, destination-LAST there;
  • and the mnemonics diverge wherever they are not coincidentally equal — `orr`/`eor`/`mvn`/`lsl`/`ldr`/`str`/`bl`/`b.eq` against `orq`/`xorq`/`notq`/`shlq`/`movq`/`call`/`je`.

★★ THE SEVEN CLAIMS THIS FIXTURE WITNESSES THAT A UNIT TEST CANNOT, each with its own way of being silently wrong:
  1. a token table where `#` is a VALUE lexes a real AArch64 gas file, and the significant `LineEnd` keeps one instruction per line (flag `\n` as EmptySpace and `ret` swallows the next line's `mov` — a wrong PARSE, not an error);
  2. the seven line-structure rules reached through `languageReferences` parse it with NO grammar of their own in this dialect — the reuse claim, measured;
  3. `.type main, %function` / `.type helper, %function` decide WHICH labels are functions, so `Lwin` and `Lfail` are BLOCKS inside `main` rather than two more functions;
  4. a NOT-TAKEN conditional branch (`b.ne Lfail`) falls through into an UNLABELED block, which the lowering has to mint as a real LIR block and wire as the jcc's second successor — the assembly names only ONE target, and getting the implicit edge wrong is invisible until it runs;
  5. a TAKEN conditional branch (`b.eq Lwin`) reaches a labelled block, and its `cond` (`ne`, `eq`) rides the SAME `TargetCondCode` vocabulary the C front-end's comparisons already use — no dialect-private condition set was minted;
  6. `bl helper` calls a second function IN THE SAME FILE and its return value is load-bearing: `main` computes 186 and helper turns it into 42;
  7. the words link into a real ELF whose entry trampoline calls `main`, and qemu-aarch64 runs it.

★★ THE ARITHMETIC AND THE BRANCHES ARE BOTH LOAD-BEARING, WHICH IS THE WHOLE POINT OF NOT WRITING `mov x0, #42; ret`. `100 - 7 = 93`, `93 * 2 = 186`, `186 - 144 = 42` — three dependent steps, the last one inside the callee. Every edge has a DISTINCT wrong answer, so a dropped one cannot hide:
  • `b.ne Lfail` wrongly TAKEN (a reversed cond-code table — `ne` and `eq` swapped) ⇒ exit 1;
  • `b.eq Lwin` wrongly NOT taken (the jcc's taken/fallthrough operands transposed) ⇒ falls into `b Lfail` ⇒ exit 1;
  • the unlabeled fallthrough block dropped or merged ⇒ the multiply never runs ⇒ `cmp x0, #186` fails ⇒ exit 1;
  • `bl helper` dropped, or its result ignored ⇒ exit 186;
  • `sub x0, x0, x1` read as two-address (`x0 = x0 - x0`) ⇒ exit 0;
  • operand order read as destinationLast ⇒ `sub x0, x0, x1` writes x1 and `mov x9, x30` writes x30 ⇒ nothing survives.

★★ `mov x9, x30` IS NOT NOISE — IT IS THE ABI, HAND-WRITTEN, WHICH IS EXACTLY WHAT THE `encode` TIER MEANS. `bl` overwrites x30, so a `main` that calls anything must preserve its own return address or return into its callee. Nothing in DSS does that for this file: `materializeCallingConvention` does not run at this tier, by design, because injecting a prologue over the one the programmer wrote is a miscompile of intent. x9 is caller-saved on AAPCS64 and `helper` does not touch it, so NO callee-saved register is clobbered anywhere in this file and the trampoline's state survives.

★ WHY THE BRANCH TARGETS ARE `Lwin`/`Lfail` AND NOT gas's USUAL `.L1`/`.L2`: a leading `.` is this dialect's `directiveIntroducer`, so `.L1:` routes to `asmDirective`. ⓘ UPDATED 2026-08-13 — that line no longer PARSES badly: the shared `asmDirective` grew an `{optional asmLabelTail}` slot and `.L1:` is now accepted by the grammar in both dialects. It is still not DEFINABLE, because the walker sends a directive node to the directive-vocabulary lookup and refuses `.L1` by name, and a dotted name is still not a legal branch-target OPERAND — so the two things this file would need are a consumer that reads a label tail on a directive node and an operand arm that opens with the introducer. Plain identifiers are equally valid gas and remain the honest choice until both land. Anchored: D-ASM-DOT-PREFIXED-LOCAL-LABELS-UNPARSEABLE (grammar half done 2026-08-13) · D-ASM-DOT-PREFIXED-LABEL-NOT-DEFINED-BY-CONSUMER · D-ASM-DOTTED-NAME-NOT-AN-OPERAND.

★★ RED-ON-DISABLE, i.e. what breaks this fixture and how: flip `operandOrder` to `destinationLast` (every three-address instruction writes the wrong register); delete any `instructions[]` row (fails loud, unknown mnemonic); change a `cond` (a branch inverts ⇒ exit 1); drop the `b.eq` token declaration (the line fails to lex, because `.` would split the mnemonic); drop either `.type` row (the labels stop being functions — `helper` becomes a block of `main` and `bl helper` has no symbol); flag `"\n"` as `EmptySpace` (the file misparses); remove the `{"rule": "root", "tier": "encode"}` row (the unit takes the full pipeline and dies at HIR).

★ THE `release` ARM, SCOPED HONESTLY. At the `encode` tier no MIR module exists, so the optimizer, the register allocator and calling-convention materialization never run — this arm therefore does NOT witness the optimizer and cannot. It pins the narrower fact that asking for `--config=release` still produces a working binary, i.e. the release configuration does not BREAK the assembly path. What prevents a `.s` from reaching the optimizer is structural (`pipelineEntry` + no MIR module to run passes over), not this arm.
